ugh early October consistently show El-Sayed leading by roughly 2 to 7 points, including surveys from Republican-leaning pollsters, and the polling average sits near 3.6 points. Most expert ratings call the race Lean D or Tilt D, though Cook, Fox News, and RealClearPolitics still rate it a tossup.\n\nMoney is a complicating factor: El-Sayed has raised more in principal funds, but outside groups have spent heavily against him, while Rogers benefits from stronger outside support. Prediction markets price El-Sayed's chances around 72-73%. The race remains genuinely competitive in a state that has been closely divided, but the weight of recent evidence favors the Democrat by a modest margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7118, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7565, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7778, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.755, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7606, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7617, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7781, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 3.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7047, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7427, "margin": 4.0}]}